BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Relativistic travel: the trip autopilot</h1>
Delta-gliders in a 300 km Earth orbit fly trips with the ideal drive's
autopilot (Relativistic Travel MFD): into orbits about Mars at 1,000 g
(500 km) and at 100,000 g (700 km; 0.85 c), to rest 1,000 km above the Moon at
10 g, past Mars 1,000 km out at 1,000 g, and to the Moon in a set time.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 51982.6685767396
  Script Tests/RelTripTest
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship T1
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET T1
  MODE Extern
  POS 4 0 -20
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 50.00
END_CAMERA

